<title>CANADA: SW Canada Prairies face frost risk Thursday night.</title>
<headline>SW Canada Prairies face frost risk Thursday night.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Thursday were forecast to see a slight to moderate risk of frost in the southwest grainbelt Thursday night, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta's foothills face a moderate risk of frost into Friday morning while a slight risk extends into central and southern Alberta and southwestern Saskatchewan as skies clear, Environment Canada's 10-day frost outlook said.</p>
<p>A slight risk of frost was forecast Saturday and Sunday mornings for an oval area extending from Yorkton, Sask., to Brandon, Man., as skies clear there.</p>
<p>A slight risk was seen in north Alberta Sept 9 and 10.</p>
<p>A slight risk was forecast for Alberta's foothills Sept 11 to 13.</p>
<p>- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
